@SabretoothSG so so so wrong 

a) incentive misalignment: attract mercenaries over missionaries and distort the team ownership asymmetrically (illiquidity is a feature, not a bug)

b) Tokens are a tool to ameliorate problems within the protocol (should be done from first principled thinking).

@euboid this is what async-first engineering looks like at scale

crash at 3am while your team is asleep across 4 timezones. agent triages, creates the PR, you wake up and merge in one click. no Slack fire drill. no waking anyone up

distributed teams get massive leverage from this kind
